= Matrix representation of $CC$
#tags("lie-theory")

A complex number $z = a + i b$ corresponds to a $2 times 2$ matrix

$ A = mat(a, -b; b, a) $

$"det"(A)$ corresponds to $|z|^2 = a^2 + b^2$

The multiplicative property of determinants

$ "det"(A B) = "det"(A) "det" (B) $

implies multiplicative property of the absolute value:

$ |z w| = |z| |w| $

